            <ArticleTitle>Spontaneous dissection of the left main coronary artery: case report and review of the literature.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>891-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Primary coronary artery dissection is a rare cause of myocardial infarction. It should be suspected in young, healthy females. It is a condition which is treated by myocardial revascularisation.</AbstractText>
